window.docContents[220].resolve({"/Appendix/#section-chapter-10-connectivity-results":{"contents":"* Connected.card_connectedComponent / connected_iff_card_connectedComponent: a\ngraph is connected iff it has exactly one connected component (counted with\nNat.card, so with no finiteness assumption).* hypercube_connected: the n-dimensional hypercube is connected.* connected_mycielskian_iff: the Mycielskian mμ[G] is connected iff G has no\nisolated vertices.* isBridge_mycielskian_iff: the bridges of mμ[G] are the edges none — u ᵣ with\nu isolated in G.* Walk.IsCycle.mem_support_iff_reachable_of_degree_le_two /\nWalk.IsCycle.toSubgraph_eq_of_degree_le_two /\nWalk.IsCycle.isHamiltonianCycle_of_degree_le_two: in a graph of maximum degree at\nmost 2, every cycle passes through every vertex of its component, and as a\nsubgraph is equal to that component, so in a connected such graph every cycle is a\nHamiltonian cycle.* pathNat₁_connected / pathNat₁_isAcyclic / pathNat₁_isTree: the infinite path\non ℕ is a tree (so every edge is a bridge).* Walk.exists_isEulerian_circuit: Euler's theorem, existence direction (in a graph\nwith finitely many edges, if all edges lie in one component and every vertex has\neven degree, there is an Eulerian circuit).* Walk.exists_isEulerian_trail_of_two_odd: in a graph with finitely many edges, if\nall edges lie in one component and exactly two vertices a ≠ b have odd degree,\nthere is an Eulerian trail from a to b.* isVertexConnected_iff_induce: G is k-vertex-connected iff it has more than\nk vertices and G.induce Sᶜ is preconnected whenever S.encard < k.* vertexConnectivity_le_edgeConnectivity: κ(G) ≤ λ(G) for every\ngraph.* brooks_two: Brooks' theorem for Δ = 2, a graph of maximum degree at most 2 is\n2-colourable unless one of its components is an odd cycle.* brooks: Brooks' theorem for Δ ≥ 3, a finite graph with maximum degree\nat most Δ and no (Δ + 1)-clique is Δ-colourable.* colorable_of_cliqueFree_of_degree_le: the same for locally finite graphs.* brooks_general: Brooks' theorem for every Δ.* isVertexConnected_two_iff: a graph is 2-vertex-connected iff it has at least\nthree vertices, is connected and has no cut vertex.* IsCutVertex.splitsAt / splitsAt_of_not_reachable: a graph splits at each of its\ncut vertices, and at every vertex if its edges lie in two different components.* colorable_of_forall_block: for n ≥ 1, a finite graph is n-colourable if\neach of its blocks is.\n\nFrom the exercises:\n\n* IsTree.degree_le_card_leaves: a finite tree has at least as many leaves as the\ndegree of any of its vertices.* IsVertexConnected.le_minDegree: a k-vertex-connected graph has minimum degree\nat least k.* IsVertexConnected.boxProd_top_bool: if G is connected and k-vertex-connected\nthen G □ K₂ is (k + 1)-vertex-connected.* hypercube_isVertexConnected / hypercube_isEdgeConnected: the n-dimensional\nhypercube is n-vertex-connected and n-edge-connected.* edgeConnectivity_le_minDegree: λ(G) ≤ δ(G) for a finite graph\nwith at least two vertices (completing Whitney's inequalities).* vertexConnectivity_hypercube / edgeConnectivity_hypercube_succ: κ(Q[n]) = n,\nand λ(Q[n + 1]) = n + 1 (while λ(Q[0]) = ⊤).* IsAcyclic.toSubgraph_blockMk: in a forest the block of an edge is the subgraph\nconsisting of that edge and its endpoints.* colorable_iff_forall_block: for n ≥ 1, a graph is n-colourable iff each of\nits blocks is.\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Appendix\u0009Results","header":"14.3.8. Chapter 10: Connectivity (Results)","id":"/Appendix/#section-chapter-10-connectivity-results"}});